    "fix round 2: address review T-1297 comment orchestrator/daemon.py:1666 [med]: When active mode is refused by the promotion gate, notify() fires on every tick for as long as the criteria stay unmet. test_active_promotion_refusal_uses_shadow asserts one notification per tick. That floods the notification channel. Also, promotion.collect re-reads the decision log on every tick in active mode. Notify only when the refusal reasons change, or once per interval.",
    "fix round 2: address review T-1297 comment orchestrator/decision_log.py:263 [med]: recent(kind, subject) scans backwards until it finds `limit` matching rows. A task normally has far fewer than 500 steering rows, so each call reads and json-parses the whole decisions.jsonl. _steering_decisions calls it once per running task per tick, which makes tick cost grow with total log size times the number of running tasks. Use a much smaller limit (only the last row and the applied rows ",
    "fix round 2: address review T-1297 comment orchestrator/promotion.py:122 [low]: Fix-round and token criteria for steering_policy are now skipped whenever active_n is 0. Active mode can therefore be promoted on shadow_n >= 20 alone. This is needed to bootstrap, but it means the fix-round criteria are only enforced after the first active row. The docs should say so. Separately, shadow_n now counts distinct root task ids instead of shadow rows, which is a stricter, unrequested c",
